# DLAP dev stack environment: superseded by the repo-root .env.example.
#
# The dev compose pair reads ONE env file, created at the repo root and passed
# explicitly (Compose does not look in the repo root on its own):
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   docker compose --env-file .env \
#     -f deployment/environments/dev/docker-compose.yml \
#     -f deployment/environments/dev/docker-compose.microservices.yml \
#     up -d --build
#
# Do not copy this file to deployment/environments/dev/.env. Compose would read
# that file automatically and you would then maintain two env files that can
# disagree, which is what this change removed.
#
# The variables this file used to list are not read by the dev stack:
# - JHIPSTER_REGISTRY_PASSWORD has a dev default in da-discovery's
#   application-dev.yml, and no JHipster registry runs.
# - JHIPSTER_SECURITY_AUTHENTICATION_JWT_BASE64_SECRET was only referenced by the
#   JHipster central-server-config files, which were removed from da-discovery.
# - The Keycloak-profile Postgres settings match no compose service.
# - COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME and COMPOSE_FILE are deliberately not set: setting them
#   would rename the Compose project and orphan the existing volumes.
# - The TLS keystore settings belong to the opt-in tls profile; see SECURITY.md.
# Social login placeholders stay in env.social-login.example.
